  "claims": [
    {
      "claim_id": "compilation-principle-claim-1",
      "verdict": "supported",
      "targets": [
        {
          "source_id": "web-computer-science-compilation-and-runtime-optimization",
          "evidence_id": "evidence-e5a7dc42e0a0"
        }
      ],
      "supporting_quotes": [
        {
          "evidence_id": "evidence-e5a7dc42e0a0",
          "exact": "Optimizations are implemented as Passes that traverse some portion of a program to either collect information or transform the program."
        }
      ],
      "observations": [
        {
          "evidence_id": "evidence-e5a7dc42e0a0",
          "subject": "LLVM optimizations",
          "predicate": "implemented_as",
          "object": "passes that traverse some portion of a program"
        }
      ],
      "applied_rule_refs": [
        "WIKI-001",
        "EVD-001",
        "VAL-001",
        "VAL-002"
      ],
      "rationale": "引文（[0,135]）完整体述 \"Optimizations are implemented as Passes that traverse some portion of a program\"，与 claim「LLVM 的优化是通过遍历程序某一部分的 passes 来实现的」逐点对应（优化=Optimizations、通过 passes 实现=implemented as Passes、遍历程序某一部分=traverse some portion of a program），属直接支持。注：请求未提供源文档全文，start/end 为相对于所给引文文本的区间。",
      "rationale_offsets": [
        {
          "source_id": "web-computer-science-compilation-and-runtime-optimization",
          "evidence_id": "evidence-e5a7dc42e0a0",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 135
        }
      ],
      "advisory": false
    },
    {
      "claim_id": "compilation-principle-claim-2",
      "verdict": "supported",
      "targets": [
        {
          "source_id": "web-computer-science-compilation-and-runtime-optimization",
          "evidence_id": "evidence-0cbb21662389"
        },
        {
          "source_id": "web-computer-science-compilation-and-runtime-optimization",
          "evidence_id": "evidence-f0fb707195ca"
        }
      ],
      "supporting_quotes": [
        {
          "evidence_id": "evidence-0cbb21662389",
          "exact": "The table below divides the passes that LLVM provides into three categories."
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "evidence-f0fb707195ca",
          "exact": "The table below divides the passes that LLVM provides into three categories. Analysis passes compute information that other passes can use or for debugging or program visualization purposes. Transform passes can use (or invalidate) the analysis passes. Transform passes all mutate the program in some way. Utility passes provide some utility but don’t otherwise fit categorization."
        }
      ],
      "observations": [
        {
          "evidence_id": "evidence-0cbb21662389",
          "subject": "LLVM passes",
          "predicate": "categorized_into_count",
          "object": "three categories"
        },
        {
          "evidence_id": "evidence-f0fb707195ca",
          "subject": "LLVM passes",
          "predicate": "categories_named",
          "object": "Analysis, Transform, Utility"
        }
      ],
      "applied_rule_refs": [
        "WIKI-001",
        "EVD-001",
        "VAL-001",
        "VAL-002"
      ],
      "rationale": "target1（[0,76]）仅说明 passes 分为三类（three categories）；target2（[0,381]）在同类描述之后依次给出 Analysis、Transform、Utility 三类及各自定义，完整支撑「三类：Analysis、Transform 和 Utility」。两条引文一致无矛盾，取并集后 claim 完全成立。注：请求未提供源文档全文，start/end 为相对于所给引文文本的区间。",
